The ML-MTP package provides the mtp pair style,
an efficient implementation of the Moment Tensor Potential (MTP)
with Kokkos and extrapolatin grade support.

MTP is a methodology for deriving a highly accurate classical
potential fit to a large archive of quantum mechanical (DFT) data.
This package was written by Zijian (Richard) Meng, Ryan Grant, and
Laurent Karim Beland at Queen's University, Canada.
